    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Find $(A+B)-C-(B-C+D)$, if\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)-C-(B-C+D) & =A+B-C-B+C-D \\\\  & =A+\\cancel{B}-\\cancel{C}-\\cancel{B}+\\cancel{C}-D \\\\  & =A-D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-D & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3-0 & -4-9 \\\\ 0-0 & 0-7 \\\\ 2-(-3) & -7-4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & -7 \\\\ 5 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
